// One conversation, shown three ways: examples/ui/10_dialogue switches
// between a DialogueBox, a DialogueBubble and a DialogueStage while it runs.
//
// $cups is the game's own variable (bound in src/main.cpp), time_of_day() its
// function, and <<quake>> its command; <<wait 1>> is Yarn's own.

title: Start
---
<<declare $cups = 0>>
Mika: Good {time_of_day()}! Tea? #line:hello #mood:happy
Sora: Only if it's the [wave]good[/wave] kind. #line:good_kind #mood:think
-> Two cups, please. #line:two
    <<set $cups = $cups + 2>>
    Mika: Two cups coming up. That makes {$cups} today. #line:coming #mood:happy
-> No tea for me. #line:none
    Mika: Suit yourself. #line:suit #mood:sad
<<wait 1>>
Sora: Did you feel that? #line:feel #mood:think
<<quake>>
Mika: [shake]The whole park shook![/shake] #line:shook #mood:sad
Sora: ...It was the kettle. #line:kettle #mood:happy
===
